# chunk-write-out-of-range: pins that `chunk-set` raises `out of range`, with
# the chunk word as `field` and the index, or [from, to] for a range, as
# `value`, for a `character` or `word` written past the end, and for any
# chunk kind at index 0, before the start or over a reversed range (chapter
# 4, Writing chunks; errors.toml). Character 4 of "abc" is just past the end,
# so it raises rather than appends. Item 0 raises though items pad. Each
# raise is at its leaf's `chunk-set`, placed at its chunk word, and each is
# caught, so the Run completes and `s` keeps "abc", since a write that fails
# leaves the root unchanged. Its Fuel, allocation and state figures are Cost
# Model 0's, as the TS Core blessed them.

> load writes identity=d95b6800842de4e47c0bea6cbc85c8464fdfe40d957da64a021ad5f82529f8c8
> deliver d1 to=writes message=go
> pump clock=2026-09-30T09:00:00Z
raise writes/r1 code="out of range" at=writes:13 pos=16:18
raise writes/r1 code="out of range" at=writes:48 pos=21:18
raise writes/r1 code="out of range" at=writes:83 pos=26:18
raise writes/r1 code="out of range" at=writes:119 pos=31:18
raise writes/r1 code="out of range" at=writes:156 pos=36:18
seg writes/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=go clause=1 fuel=215 alloc=732 state=602 end=return
run writes/r1 outcome=completed delivery=d1 handler=go fuel=215 alloc=732
pumped state=idle fuel=215

> vars
vars writes s="abc" pastEnd=["out of range", "character", 4] wordPastEnd=["out of range", "word", 2] itemZero=["out of range", "item", 0] beforeStart=["out of range", "character", -4] reversed=["out of range", "character", [3, 2]]
